From 6a7300cc39bac29a886b0629eddcbf1955289971 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Henning Hollermann <laclaro@mail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 00:33:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] Add OpenGL ES 2.0 renderer support (USE_OPENGLES2)

Adds a USE_OPENGLES2 option for GPUs limited to GLES 2.0 / GLSL ES 1.00,
such as the Mali-450 in the Vero 4K+. With it enabled (on top of
USE_OPENGLES):

- shaders are generated as GLSL ES 1.00 (#version 100, attribute/varying,
  texture2D, gl_FragColor); template fixes: no bvec mix(), no
  textureSize(), no dynamic uniform-array indexing in fragment shaders,
  no float suffixes, no local variable shadowing its function
- gl_FragDepth is unavailable, so the per-draw prim depth is applied in
  the vertex shader instead
- unsized texture formats and GL_OES_packed_depth_stencil attached to
  both depth and stencil points; no VAOs, no MSAA, no depth readback
- framebuffer copies and MSAA resolves draw a textured quad instead of
  using glBlitFramebuffer, with glCopyTexImage2D for the window surface,
  restoring the renderer's cached GL state afterwards
- SDL requests an ES 2.0 context and ImGui uses its ES2 backend

Shader compile/link failures now print the driver log and shader source,
and no longer overflow a fixed 1024-byte log buffer. mCurrentTile and
mCurrentShaderProgram are now initialized.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
